      "math_academy_id": "q-149673",
      "knowledge_point_id": "f4312c28-e298-5185-9009-e6ca243175fd",
      "knowledge_point": "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules",
      "problem": "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{18}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}(3{a}_{ij}+2{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{18}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{a}_{ij}=50,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{18}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{ij}=20.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying these rules to the given sum, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{18}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}(3{a}_{ij}+2{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{18}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}3{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{18}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}2{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =3{\\sum }_{i=1}^{18}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{a}_{ij}+2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{18}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 50+2\\cdot 20 \\\\  & =150+40 \\\\  & =190.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
