      "knowledge_point": "Applying the Sum and Constant Multiple Rules",
      "problem": "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1+{a}_{ij}+2{b}_{ij})\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}=25,\\,{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij}=20.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The sum and constant multiple rules for double summations state that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({a}_{ij}+{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{ij}, \\\\ {\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}k{a}_{ij} & =k{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{ij}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the sum rule to the given double summation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1+{a}_{ij}+2{b}_{ij}) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}2{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)+{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{a}_{ij}+2{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}{b}_{ij} \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)+25+40 \\\\  & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)+65.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}1=mn,\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}1)+65 & =8\\cdot 10+65 \\\\  & =80+65 \\\\  & =145.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{10}(1+{a}_{ij}+2{b}_{ij})=145.\n$$",
