      "problem": "Find the value of the double sum\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({a}_{i}-1)({b}_{j}+1)\n$$\n\ngiven that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{a}_{i}=12,\\,{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j}=5.\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The product rule for double summations states that\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{a}_{i}{b}_{j}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{a}_{i}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{b}_{j}.\n$$\n\nSo, using the product rule for double summations, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({a}_{i}-1)({b}_{j}+1) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}({a}_{i}-1){\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({b}_{j}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the rules for single summations, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}({a}_{i}-1){\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}({b}_{j}+1) & =({\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}{a}_{i}-{\\sum }_{i=1}^{10}1)\\cdot ({\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}{b}_{j}+{\\sum }_{j=1}^{20}1) \\\\  & =(12-10)\\cdot (5+20) \\\\  & =(2)\\cdot (25) \\\\  & =50.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
